Subject: [PATCH] dwc2: kick the root-hub status poll on port interrupts
Upstream-Status: Pending

dwc2 does not set uses_new_polling and never calls
usb_hcd_poll_rh_status() from its port interrupt, so the root hub's
status URB is only completed by usbcore's rh_timer, which fires every
250ms aligned to jiffies/(HZ/4) ("The USB 2.0 spec says 256 ms. This is
close enough", hcd.c). A port connect is therefore noticed by the hub
thread with a uniformly random 0-250ms delay.

For a normal plug-in that is fine. For a head unit that has just
swapped roles into device mode and waits ~200ms for its bus reset it
is a coin toss, and it shows in captures on a NAC Wave 2: same kernel,
same head unit, the reset started 122ms after the connect in one boot
(head unit enumerated) and had not started 250ms after the connect in
the next (head unit gone).

Do what ehci, ohci and musb do: call usb_hcd_poll_rh_status() when the
port interrupt fired, after hsotg->lock is released. The root-hub URB
completes immediately and hub_irq() kicks the hub workqueue.

Car (NAC Wave 2): hub thread on the port 0.4ms after "Port Connect
Detected".

---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c
@@ -2203,6 +2203,7 @@
 {
 	u32 gintsts, dbg_gintsts;
 	irqreturn_t retval = IRQ_HANDLED;
+	bool port_change = false;
 
 	if (!dwc2_is_controller_alive(hsotg)) {
 		dev_warn(hsotg->dev, "Controller is dead\n");
@@ -2243,8 +2244,10 @@
 			dwc2_rx_fifo_level_intr(hsotg);
 		if (gintsts & GINTSTS_NPTXFEMP)
 			dwc2_np_tx_fifo_empty_intr(hsotg);
-		if (gintsts & GINTSTS_PRTINT)
+		if (gintsts & GINTSTS_PRTINT) {
 			dwc2_port_intr(hsotg);
+			port_change = true;
+		}
 		if (gintsts & GINTSTS_HCHINT)
 			dwc2_hc_intr(hsotg);
 		if (gintsts & GINTSTS_PTXFEMP)
@@ -2262,5 +2265,19 @@
 
 	spin_unlock(&hsotg->lock);
 
+	/*
+	 * Hand root-hub port changes to usbcore now rather than leaving them
+	 * for its 250ms status poll. Without this, the time from a port
+	 * connect to the hub thread even looking at the port is uniformly
+	 * random between 0 and 250ms, since dwc2 does not use
+	 * usb_hcd_poll_rh_status() the way ehci/ohci/musb do on a port
+	 * change. Cheap at every other HCD, fatal here: a head unit that has
+	 * just swapped roles into device mode waits only ~200ms for the bus
+	 * reset before it gives up. Called outside hsotg->lock: the root-hub
+	 * URB completion runs hub_irq(), which does not re-enter the HCD.
+	 */
+	if (port_change)
+		usb_hcd_poll_rh_status(dwc2_hsotg_to_hcd(hsotg));
+
 	return retval;
 }
